## 1. Game Overview
- **What:** browser deck-building roguelike (landscape-first PWA), "feels like Slay the Spire to play, looks like a dark, painted MTG-like world you climb through" (VISION.md).
- **North star (Spencer 10-08):** rival Slay the Spire and beat it on **fun (#1)** and **visual impressiveness (#2)**. If fun and looks conflict, fun wins.
- **Pitch / world (design/lore/LORE-BIBLE.md v3, locked):** climb the Drowned Stair to the Pale Lighthouse. The lamp is a lure; under the Pale Sea the Undermoon swallowed the rising sun and the last Lampbearer, Ilse Harrow. The player is about to repeat it.
- **Tone:** dark coastal-gothic, grim and weathered, "beauty with a hook in it"; dawn is a lie. Original names/art only (no StS/MTG names, text, icons or art).
- **Scope now:** **Act 1 live; Act 2 + Act 3 now IN SCOPE (Spencer 2026-10-15, task CLAUDE_TASK_ACT2_BUILD; spec studio/design/ACT2-BUILD-PLAN.md).** Full game (3 acts, ~75 cards/hero, 186 relics, 48 potions, 25+ events, Ascension, daily runs) is the design target. Acts 2/3 stay behind the live flag (ACT_COUNT=1) until 9/10 art + sims pass.
- **Platform:** Spencer's Samsung Galaxy S24 (landscape, CSS ~832x384). Possible Google Play release later.
