## 3. Technical Constraints & Stack
- **Engine:** none — vanilla JavaScript ES modules + HTML/CSS, served by `node serve.js` (`npm start`). PWA: `manifest.webmanifest`, `sw.js` (cache prefix `tidebound-`, bump per release). `version.js` holds the version.
- **Layout (repo `/workspace/game`):**
  - `src/core/` (bus, registry, state, timing) · `src/engine/` (combat, cards, effects, run, preview, lamplight) · `src/data/` (classes, enemies, encounters, relics, potions, events, keywords, environments; `data/cards/act1/`, `data/generated/` = generated, edit the generator) · `src/ui/` (render + feature modules) · `src/assets.js` (asset map) · `src/save.js` (save v4 with migration), `src/progress.js`.
  - `css/` (style.css + feature sheets) · `art/v2/` (all live art) · `audio/`, `fonts/`, `icons/` · `tests/` (*.cjs/*.js) · `tools/` (generators, `test-lock.sh`, `art-review.sh`) · `design/` (design docs) · `playtests/`.
- **Manifests:** tiles `art/v2/ui/tiles.json` (new slots via `tools/make-tiles-manifest.cjs`), sprites `art/v2/sprites/sprites.json`; placeholders wired through the manifest so real art drops in with no code change.
- **Tests / QC:** `npm test` = mech.js, bugs_repro, behaviour --engine, phase1, lore22, test.js, shot.js, hand-peek, choice-taps (~22 min). Run heavy ones through `tools/test-lock.sh`. Definition of done: mech + phase1 + shot green + task's own test, no stale tests.
- **Deploy:** `bash /workspace/game-deploy/deploy.sh` (separate dir, never edits the game tree). Clean commit + tag; SW cache bump in deploy copy; live smoke after push. Aborts without changelogs.
- **Git:** integrator (Clovis) merges task branches to `main`; never deploy a dirty tree. Each task: `git -C /workspace/game worktree add /workspace/wt/<task> -b task/<task>`; explicit `git add <files>`; never `git add -A`, stash or wipe in shared trees; checkpoint commits ≤30 min.
- **File rules:** stay inside the task's "Files it may touch"; one coder per file area at a time; tasks that stale a test fix it in the same commit.
