### 13.10 Piece-rig idle system (v0.6.27 LIVE 10-15 21:55 PT, build deploy-20261015-215507, branch clovis/rig-idle -> release/v0.6.27 @7eea056 on v0.6.26; 27 rigs = 4 heroes + 23 enemies, 7.8 MB, precache 123.8 MB; live proof studio/qc/rig-live-v0.6.27.png; phase1.js failure is pre-existing on base)
- **What it is:** characters idle as ~10-15 painted pieces (base + head, torso, cloaks, staff, lantern...) moved on pivots/parents by sine channels, instead of one bent sprite (the "jello" look). Rig files live in `art/v2/rigs/<spriteId>/<spriteId>.rig.json` + `pieces/*.webp`; `art/v2/rigs/index.json` lists rigs and every shipped file (so tools/gen-precache.cjs puts them in the offline precache). Format spec: `design/RIG-FORMAT.md` (copy of /workspace/idle-test/chars/RIG-FORMAT.md). Reference maths + renderer: /workspace/idle-test/chars/tools/rigmath.py; sources/exports: /workspace/idle-test/chars/<name>/; importer: `python3 tools/build-rigs.py [name...]` (tints glow masks, writes index.json; never edits sources).
- **Runtime:** `src/ui/rig-math.js` (pure pose maths, matches rigmath.py to 1e-13, test fixture tests/fixtures/rig-pose-golden.json) and `src/ui/rig.js` (DOM compositor). `syncCombatAnimations()` (anim.js) calls `syncRigs()` after every render: each `.hero/.en .spr-slot` whose `data-asset` sprite id has a rig gets a `.rig` child (pieces are absolutely positioned `<img class=rp>` in a sprite-pixel space scaled by figure width / sprite width, moved with `transform: matrix()` only), the slot gets `.rigged` and the plain `img.spr` is `visibility:hidden` (kept in layout so place.js/targeting still read its rect). One shared rAF loop animates all live rigs.
- **Keeps working unchanged:** attack lunge, hit flash/shake, telegraph, death ghosts (ghost() clones the `.fig` including the frozen-pose `.rig`), victory finale, targeting (rig is pointer-events:none, taps hit `.fig/.en`), contact shadow (`.shadow` is a sibling), rim/stage filter (same filter rules copied onto `.rig` in css/anim.css). Hit-stop: `freezeIdle()` (vfx.js) now also calls `rigFreeze()` which holds the rig clock for the stop and then resumes (no jump).
- **Fallbacks (no rig => nothing changes):** sprite id not in index.json, index/rig/image fetch fails, `?rig=0` or localStorage `rig-off=1`, reduced motion (JS `enabled()` false => no rigs, static sprite), screen not combat. The old `combat-breathe` CSS sway still drives every unrigged figure.
- **Performance rules:** transform-only updates (no layout); loop stops when `document.hidden`, restarts on visibility; desync per figure by hashing the enemy uid (`hash01`) added to the loop phase; more than 4 live rigs start at 30 fps; adaptive tiers (60 -> 30 -> 15 -> frozen) step up if the measured frame spacing stays > 22/30 ms (2.5 s grace after attach); LRU keeps at most 10 decoded rigs in memory. Test hooks: `window.__rig` (rigStats, setTier(n,lock), live, pose).
- **Adding a character:** drop `<name>/<name>.rig.json` + `pieces/` in /workspace/idle-test/chars, run `python3 tools/build-rigs.py <name>`, then `node tools/gen-precache.cjs --write`; sprite id (sprites.json key) must equal the folder name and rig.sprite.w/h must equal the sprite size (tests/rig-idle.cjs checks both). Budget: all rigs < 10 MB (tests/rig-idle.cjs enforces); precache total must stay < 140 MB (tests/precache-coverage.cjs).
- **Known limits:** glow layers are faint tinted additive images (`mix-blend-mode:plus-lighter`), not clipped to the silhouette; drop-shadow filter group is re-composited each animated frame (cheap on GPU phones, heavy on software rendering, hence the tiers); not yet measured on a real S24. Tests: tests/rig-idle.cjs (in npm test).

