- **Fix (src/ui/render.js `laneOf(n,vw)`, used by enemyX/enemyHTML/remainsHTML/badges):** 1 and 2 enemies keep the old lane exactly. 3+ start the lane further left (first-centre fractions: 3 .60, 4 .53, 5 .48, 6 .44; right edge still .98) and the SPRITE width cap becomes cell*1.3 minus 1.2% (neighbours may overlap up to ~35%), while HP plates/intents keep the plain cell width (`enemyMaxWidth`, `--bw`) so plates never collide. Feet stay on the shared ground line (heights are only capped, never moved), the hero, hand layout and 1-2 enemy fights are untouched.
- **Measured at S24 832x384 (sprite px, before -> after):** Act 1: 3 pods 82x104 -> 89x114; 4 foes (gull gull wisp slug) 54x34 -> 147x92 (gull); 6 foes 30x19 -> 110x69 (gull). Act 2: 3 foes (pylon, 2 ghostcannon) ghostcannon 80x24 -> 177x53; 4 foes 53x16 -> 147x44; 6 foes 30x9 -> 110x33; pylon/deckshade/mortar 31x51-95 -> 69x114 / 110x91. All fully on screen (min left 311, max right 828), max neighbour overlap 36%.
- New test tests/battle-room-measure.cjs (prints sizes for 1/2/3/4/6 foes Act 1 + ?act=2; with CHECK=1 asserts on-screen, shared feet, overlap <=45%). Shots: studio/qc/battle-room-v1/{before,after}/. If bosses/elites in crowds look too big or cluttered, tune LANE_A / the 1.3 factor in render.js.

